WEBVTT

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:28.760
good job of lettering I ever saw in my life

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:30.450
Save much.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:31.700
That'll be $10, please.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.390
Yes, sir, you're a real artist with that stuff.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:35.270
A real artist.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:36.480
Tent fish.

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:38.950
I'll mail you a check tomorrow, pal.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.570
I'd rather have the money today.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:42.940
Well, you're never going to get any place

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:43.940
if you don't trust people.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.140
You know, I've been around a long time, buddy.

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:47.760
You don't belong here.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.000
You really belong on Broadway.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:49.560
Yeah?

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.920
Yeah, and I think the walk would do you good.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:54.360
I take it off for $5.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.830
No, but you might do. Are you available?

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.170
Oh, for you. Anytime, Miss, uh...

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:07.210
Lawrence. Kathy Lawrence.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:08.830
Kathy, you're my first client.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.320
Shall we celebrate by my carrying you across the threshold?

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.580
Oh, no. It's such a nice day, I think I'll walk.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.290
You take the comfortable chair.

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:27.680
Thank you. I think you'll do fine.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:29.960
You're a doll to say so, but...

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.040
Just what do I do fine?

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:35.210
I'm a reporter on the San Francisco Tribune.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.450
I'm down here on a story, and I need some help.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.350
I'm your man.

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:41.350
I shadow, investigate, prove and disprove suspicions,

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:44.000
and dance divinely, all at reasonable rates.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.020
I can't pay you a fee.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:47.690
This changes the picture.

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:50.170
But I'll make you a business proposition.

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:52.310
Shoot.

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:56.370
I presume you know this person.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.970
Sure, Judge Finley Drake, or ex-judge.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.200
since every cop in the state started looking for him.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.260
I think I know where he's hiding.

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:10.570
There's a $10,000 reward riding on Judge Drake's head.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.480
How would you like to have half of it?

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:21.070
I have a pretty strong hunch that the judge

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.190
is hiding in a local private sanitarium,

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:28.130
the La Siesta for mental cases, run by a Dr. Clifford Porter,

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:29.970
former state medical officer, and...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.080
and a good friend of Drake's.

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.160
Are you good at hunches like this?

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.600
Actually, this is more than a hunch.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.120
That's Madge Bennett, the judge's girlfriend.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:42.810
Can I say?

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:45.790
That picture is 10 years old.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.790
Everybody thought Madge left San Francisco with a judge,

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:51.770
but I saw her in town a few days ago

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:52.870
and followed her down here.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:55.440
Last night, she went to the sanitarium.

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:57.690
Why don't you give this information

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.510
to your paper or to the police?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.500
Well, because I can't prove that he's there until somebody actually sees him in the place.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.320
And where do I fit in?

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.520
I want you to go in as a patient.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:12.230
You just say I'm crazy?

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:14.060
It's the only way you can get in there.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:16.460
Honey, I'm not that hungry.

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:20.650
Chance to make a lot of money and put the judge and his friends in jail.

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:25.940
No, don't go away mad, but I'm not getting myself locked up in any nuthouse on a hunch.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:27.720
Si.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:30.740
Our business is over.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:33.140
How about you and me doing a tour in the local pool rooms?

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:34.720
So sorry.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:35.780
Pool isn't my game.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:38.150
You're not my man.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.340
I'll find someone else.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:07.200
Hello.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.100
I come bearing news and apologies.

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:12.110
All right, come in.

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:23.270
I decided to check on your girlfriend just out of curiosity.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:24.360
Oh, really?

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:28.120
She went back to that sanitarium again last night,

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:29.970
and she didn't go in through the front entrance.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:31.730
I knew you'd check on her.

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:33.330
That's why I left the picture in your office.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:34.330
Well, what do you know?

00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:37.930
Say, I bet that's why you left that scrap of hotel

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.680
car in that stationery, so I'd know where to find you, too.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:42.950
I suppose that makes you a clever detective,

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:43.850
figuring that out.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:48.390
I've, uh, I've come to accept your proposition.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:50.580
What's our first move?

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:55.470
We'll need a close relative to ask for your commitment.

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:58.600
I'm sure my relatives would be delighted if I had any.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:07:59.980
Are you mad?

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:00.740
No.

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:08.080
Would you mind being married to me?

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:09.480
Twist my arm.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.600
The point is we'll just say we're married

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.480
to get you into the sanitarium.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:17.710
OK, if we can make a deal for after I'm out.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:20.330
This is strictly a business proposition.

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:23.310
Your part in this deal is to play a mentally unbalanced

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:23.710
husband.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:26.570
Who's always kissing his wife, in public, in private,

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:27.390
all the time.

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:29.430
We can figure out a better act than that.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:29.970
Oh, no.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.650
No, I think we'd both be awfully good enough.

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:35.110
Mr. Stewart, I'd love to spend the rest of the day

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:37.630
trying to outmaneuver you, but we have work to do.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:41.930
What's this?

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:42.870
Research.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:45.520
You have to decide what kind of a mental case

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:48.380
you're going to be, a paranoiac, a schizophrenic,

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.680
a manic depressive, and then we'll

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:51.860
have to decide on your name.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.060
What's wrong with the name I've got?

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:55.680
Ross Stewart.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:56.940
I think it's kind of pretty.

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:59.720
Well, it's a beautiful name, but with your retiring

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:03.100
there's just a chance that somebody in town might know you.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:05.480
So I think we'd better change it to something simple,

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:07.100
like Harry or...

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:09.790
Horton. I like names that go together. Harry, Horton.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:13.380
All right, Mr. Horton. And you can be an unemployed salesman.

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:15.420
Well, you hit the nail right on the head with that unemployed.

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:20.330
Now, tell me, Mrs. H., what's supposed to be the matter with me?

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:22.060
Well, that's what we've got to figure out.

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:25.290
I thought I'd take you downtown to the state psychiatrist,

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:28.170
tell him that you've been acting queerly and ask his advice.

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:29.970
And you'll have to know how...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.740
to act so he can recognize the symptoms.

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:33.610
Well, now, here's one I kind of like.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:35.610
The symptoms of the manic depressive

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:38.270
consist mainly of emotional disturbances, depression,

00:09:39.130 --> 00:09:42.890
anxiety, elation, rage, a variety of happy and sad moods.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.700
You think you can be sad for a minute?

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:46.860
Oh, I can be very sad.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:48.120
I can even be unattractive.

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:51.330
You know, you could tell him that I beat you one minute

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:52.830
and kiss you madly.

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:55.430
I'm not so sure you're not really

00:09:55.430 --> 00:09:58.110
insane with that kissing fixation of yours.

00:09:58.830 --> 00:09:59.970
Maybe you've got a better way to go.

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:08.510
Is there something troubling you, Mr. Horton?

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:11.600
Something you're afraid to tell your wife about?

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:16.310
Is there something troubling you, Mr. Horton?

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:17.690
I got nothing to say.

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:19.670
It was her idea to come here, not mine.

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.660
We want to help you, but you must cooperate.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:25.100
Nobody can help me. Nobody can help anybody.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:31.910
I don't know what to do for him, doctor.

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:33.450
He's getting worse all the time.

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:36.630
Just what would you like me to do, Mrs. Horton?

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:38.230
I don't know.

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.210
I wanted your advice.

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:47.100
Could you bring your husband back here Wednesday

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.660
at 10 o'clock?

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:50.300
I suppose so.

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:50.840
Why?

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.810
I'll examine him and make a report to the court.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:56.480
If the court ailments concur, they'll

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:58.440
recommend that he be confined to the state asylum

00:10:58.440 --> 00:10:58.860
for treatment.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:10:59.280
Oh, no.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:00.620
No, what?

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:04.460
I wouldn't want him in the state asylum.

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:07.180
I thought possibly a private sanitarium.

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:09.860
Private sanitariums are an expensive proposition.

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:12.260
But if you feel you can afford it, by all means,

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:12.980
place him in one.

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:14.510
Most of them are very good.

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:17.260
How would I go about it, doctor?

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:19.640
Is there any way you can help?

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:20.880
Certainly.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.960
I'll write a letter stating that, in my opinion,

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:25.500
your husband needs professional attention.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:28.230
A letter from me will more or less

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:29.610
force them to admit him immediately.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:32.410
Private sanatoriums are very crowded today.

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:37.240
Miss Cook, would you come in, please?

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:38.360
I want to dictate a letter.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.960
I'm sure in time your husband will respond.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.000
on the treatment, Mrs. Horton?

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:02.930
How much time, Dr. Porter?

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.510
How long do you think you'll have to stay here?

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:06.370
That's impossible to say, which you

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:09.030
must be prepared to leave him in our care as long as necessary.

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:13.780
I hope he'll be allowed to move around to be with the others.

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:15.460
He'll live quite a normal life.

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:17.770
Our patients are allowed to mingle freely

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:19.310
in routine everyday relationships.

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:23.890
About the cost, doctor, I can't afford a private room.

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:26.290
We have a bed open in a three-man ward.

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:27.130
I'll assign him there.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:28.430
I'll be fine.

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:31.820
Hopps.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.010
I want you to be good, dear.

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:35.190
Do everything they tell you.

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:42.590
This is Mr. Hopps, one of our attendants.

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:43.670
Mrs. Horton.

00:12:44.020 --> 00:12:44.620
Mrs. Horton.

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:45.440
And her husband.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:46.220
Mrs. Horton.

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:48.740
Mr. Horton is going to be with us a while, Hopps.

00:12:48.820 --> 00:12:49.940
Fix him up in Ward 10.

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:50.660
Yes, sir.

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:52.330
Will you come with me?

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:13.400
So you think you've got to be for the world.

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:26.950
Here's your bed.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.760
Well, you hang your clothes in your locker here every night.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.010
I'll have to take your tie, everything you've got in your pockets.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:38.580
You can keep the cigarettes.

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:40.380
What about matches? How do I get a light?

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:41.840
Well, you can only smoke in the day room.

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:43.320
We don't like patients to have matches.

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:45.210
Give me your suspenders.

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:46.920
How do I keep my pants up?

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.520
Sorry, we have to take all these things away from depressives.

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:51.960
We don't want any accidents.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:55.020
Mr. Purvis, uh, Mr. Horton.

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:57.930
Another poor fish caught in the porter net.

00:13:58.250 --> 00:13:59.490
Don't unpack your bag, Horton.

00:13:59.610 --> 00:13:59.970
Get out of this.

00:14:01.490 --> 00:14:04.410
Why do you want to make trouble for yourself, Mr. Purvis?

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:06.330
I keep telling you, you're gonna get into trouble

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:07.190
if you don't keep still.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:13.030
He looks strong, put him to work with you, Hopps.

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:14.030
Yes, sir.

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:16.890
Orton, ask the noble doctor if the patient helpers

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:17.950
get paid for their work.

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:20.740
It's part of the treatment to keep you occupied

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:21.680
in some useful task.

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:22.380
Treatment?

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:25.310
Making the patients work saves hiring janitors.

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:27.560
Mr. Purvis, I've warned you before.

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:29.980
If this keeps on, it may become necessary to...

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.240
to transfer you to the Locked Ward.

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:37.890
I'll have to take your shoes, too.

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:39.010
I'll bring you some slippers.

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:40.570
Whose bed is that?

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:41.670
Mr. Quist.

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:44.300
He's a very nervous fellow, likes to be let alone,

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:45.620
so don't bother him.

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:46.780
He ought to be left alone.

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:47.900
What about our nerves?

00:14:48.710 --> 00:14:50.250
Wait till you try to sleep tonight.

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:54.140
Wait till you try to sleep.

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:55.340
Why don't you take it easy?

00:14:55.730 --> 00:14:58.010
Why don't you have a backbone enough to do something

00:14:58.010 --> 00:14:59.290
about this place, Hopps?

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:02.280
You're going to make trouble for yourself.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.260
You know what a rotten disgrace it is.

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:06.820
Why don't you tell somebody on the outside?

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:10.200
People on the outside aren't much interested in us on the inside,

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.020
inmates or attendants.

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:27.920
What's wrong with the new guy?

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:29.810
He's a depressive.

00:15:30.920 --> 00:15:32.420
He'll be all right after a little rest.

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:35.440
I'll make sure he gets a good rest.

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:55.990
Chap.

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:41.930
Stop it.

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:47.240
He's just giving a champ a workout?

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:49.620
I've told you a dozen times not to abuse the patients.

00:17:09.370 --> 00:17:11.150
You screaming monkey? Cut it out. Quit hitting him.

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:14.580
Get back in bed. You too, Purvis, or you'll get the same.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:16.800
What kind of a joint is this?

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:20.430
Look, no boy, let me give you some advice.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.380
Don't stick your nose in what's none of your business.

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:25.250
Now get back in bed.

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:32.560
And stay there.

00:17:54.508 --> 00:17:56.568
He's the one you've got to watch around here.

00:17:57.676 --> 00:17:59.076
You came here to be cured?

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:01.740
You're more likely to be killed.

00:18:20.508 --> 00:18:22.328
Come here anytime you're not supposed to be working.

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:04.700
Good day, sir.

00:19:05.436 --> 00:19:06.276
I wonder...

00:19:06.492 --> 00:19:08.492
if by chance you're a chess player.

00:19:09.948 --> 00:19:10.588
I'm afraid I'm not.

00:19:10.728 --> 00:19:12.268
Oh, that is unfortunate.

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:14.640
Please pardon the intrusion.

00:19:15.772 --> 00:19:16.612
Okay.

00:19:23.932 --> 00:19:27.052
Topper's been trying for three years to get somebody to play chess with him.

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:29.460
Three years? He's been here that long? What's wrong with him?

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:30.800
It's a fire bug.

00:19:32.428 --> 00:19:34.048
Nearly burned up a whole neighborhood once.

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:36.460
Otherwise, he's okay.

00:19:37.452 --> 00:19:39.092
Used to be a pretty big businessman, they say.

00:19:39.884 --> 00:19:41.084
How long the rest of these men been here?

00:19:41.708 --> 00:19:42.068
Oh.

00:19:42.348 --> 00:19:43.668
three months to a year or more.

00:19:45.132 --> 00:19:46.212
You won't be here that long.

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:49.500
I don't think there's much wrong with you.

00:19:51.212 --> 00:19:51.712
I, uh,

00:19:53.004 --> 00:19:54.524
I met another attendant last night.

00:19:55.756 --> 00:19:56.156
Larson.

00:19:56.972 --> 00:19:58.352
Just stay away from him all you can.

00:19:59.340 --> 00:19:59.960
Mind your own business.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:03.980
around here and you get along better that's all i've heard so far what kind of a joint is this

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:08.440
yeah i gotta get back to work

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:04.590
Where do you think you're going?

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:05.940
Just looking around.

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:13.000
Is that a locked ward?

00:21:13.920 --> 00:21:16.140
That's where you'll wind up if you don't behave yourself.

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:19.010
You're going back where you belong.

00:21:20.830 --> 00:21:22.010
You're going back where you belong.

00:21:58.220 --> 00:21:59.970
Just start by one of the.

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:04.670
Frankly, Judge, I'm beginning to resent your sending for me

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:05.850
at all hours of the day and night.

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:08.010
After all, I'm doing you the favor.

00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:12.310
It'd still be a small-time quack if I hadn't given you a break.

00:22:12.530 --> 00:22:14.370
I'm more than repaying that break right now.

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:16.280
I'm risking everything keeping you here.

00:22:16.880 --> 00:22:17.660
It's a short risk.

00:22:19.550 --> 00:22:21.710
My boys will be here as soon as things cool off.

00:22:22.060 --> 00:22:24.480
Suppose these men of yours are picked up by the police and talk.

00:22:25.710 --> 00:22:27.770
Men working for me can't afford to talk.

00:22:28.260 --> 00:22:29.160
I hope you're right.

00:22:31.020 --> 00:22:32.160
Mighty fine cigar.

00:22:33.350 --> 00:22:34.610
Don't be so appreciative.

00:22:35.900 --> 00:22:37.720
With the money I'm paying you to stay here,

00:22:37.780 --> 00:22:39.860
you can afford a truckload of those cigars.

00:22:44.720 --> 00:22:45.380
Yes, sir. Good luck.

00:22:46.770 --> 00:22:47.510
To both of us.

00:23:19.090 --> 00:23:24.420
Don't lose your hammer. This isn't a steal.

00:23:24.790 --> 00:23:26.030
What a deal. All this and...

00:23:30.860 --> 00:23:47.500
I haven't seen anyone who could possibly be Judge Drake.

00:23:47.930 --> 00:23:49.530
There was a rumor that he was seen in Florida.

00:23:49.850 --> 00:23:52.580
Florida? You mean, maybe I'm in here just for laughs?

00:23:52.740 --> 00:23:54.130
No, no, the police say it was just...

00:23:55.340 --> 00:23:57.640
Anyway, Madge Bennett came here again Thursday night.

00:23:57.920 --> 00:23:59.970
She had a briefcase. Obviously, she...

00:24:00.560 --> 00:24:03.140
Just spot her and find out where she goes.

00:24:03.900 --> 00:24:06.320
You know, if Drake's in disguise, it may be kind of tough to recognize her.

00:24:07.150 --> 00:24:08.550
I thought of that, sir. I brought you a present.

00:24:08.750 --> 00:24:17.670
I thought if you kept looking at it, you could see through any disguise.

00:24:19.670 --> 00:24:20.750
You're a real smart kid.

00:24:20.930 --> 00:24:26.740
Good afternoon, Mrs. Horton.

00:24:27.140 --> 00:24:28.140
Oh, good afternoon, Doctor.

00:24:29.170 --> 00:24:29.970
Yeah, I see what you have in your...

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:30.440
Can I take your hand, please?

00:24:34.070 --> 00:24:37.100
Let Dr. Porter see it. He'll give it back to you.

00:24:37.260 --> 00:24:49.400
A nice picture, Mrs. Orton.

00:24:49.640 --> 00:24:50.380
Thank you, Doctor.

00:25:01.050 --> 00:25:03.010
You're quite a performance. Your talents are amazing.

00:25:03.230 --> 00:25:03.550
Thanks.

00:25:04.740 --> 00:25:06.650
Do you think you've seen all of the inmates?

00:25:06.850 --> 00:25:08.100
I've got the place pretty well.

00:25:08.460 --> 00:25:10.380
I'll accept the locked ward. They haven't let me in there.

00:25:11.160 --> 00:25:12.320
When can you get a look in there?

00:25:12.620 --> 00:25:16.360
Give me time, honey. You know, they don't exactly have conducted tours around here.

00:25:17.950 --> 00:25:21.720
No. Anything I can bring you the next time I come?

00:25:22.460 --> 00:25:23.280
A couple of steaks.

00:25:24.380 --> 00:25:26.300
Oh, you don't look as though you're suffering too much.

00:25:28.860 --> 00:25:29.360
You're not...

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:31.340
You're not forcing me on the outside, are you?

00:25:31.560 --> 00:25:32.360
Running around with other men?

00:25:33.170 --> 00:25:34.410
That is none of your business.

00:25:34.550 --> 00:25:35.210
I'm your husband.

00:25:36.210 --> 00:25:36.990
Only in here.

00:25:37.900 --> 00:25:38.720
You're getting used to the...

00:25:44.700 --> 00:25:45.960
Talk about that when it is all.

00:25:53.900 --> 00:25:55.640
I've been looking a long time for a rich man.

00:25:56.000 --> 00:25:57.290
No, honey, isn't it?

00:25:59.260 --> 00:25:59.980
Wait a minute, that's me.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:02.310
I'll be worth five grand myself.

00:26:03.200 --> 00:26:14.480
You look only half work to death.

00:26:15.570 --> 00:26:16.650
How do you like our little restaurant?

00:26:18.220 --> 00:26:21.920
It's over time, Chris.

00:26:28.790 --> 00:26:29.810
Supposedly for the violence.

00:26:31.600 --> 00:26:32.560
Anybody up there now?

00:26:33.230 --> 00:26:34.050
Couple of violence.

00:26:34.270 --> 00:26:35.270
They're kept there all the time.

00:26:40.680 --> 00:26:41.720
Restraint, they call it.

00:26:44.770 --> 00:26:48.060
It's trouble to try and cure them with any kind of treatment.

00:26:48.300 --> 00:26:52.060
You heard of the isolation room they've got there, too?

00:26:53.060 --> 00:26:55.170
Air room, padded walls.

00:26:55.800 --> 00:26:56.740
They throw you a blanket.

00:26:57.260 --> 00:26:58.180
You sleep on the floor.

00:26:59.060 --> 00:26:59.920
Oh, yeah.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:02.840
Yes, this is a very high-class sanitarium.

00:27:03.470 --> 00:27:05.710
Fine care and treatment you get here.

00:27:06.080 --> 00:27:08.620
You pay extra well to be treated like a dog!

00:27:09.670 --> 00:27:12.480
Try and complain about it. Try and protest about anything.

00:27:12.580 --> 00:27:14.040
And what do you get? I'll tell you what you get!

00:27:14.140 --> 00:27:16.480
That extra special treatment! They go to your left!

00:27:16.660 --> 00:27:18.180
Take care to keep your mouth shut!

00:27:38.510 --> 00:27:40.500
Wake up, right?

00:28:49.770 --> 00:28:50.390
He didn't tell me he got enough.

00:28:50.870 --> 00:28:51.890
Yeah, a fight with Larson.

00:28:53.010 --> 00:28:53.940
He didn't do it.

00:28:53.960 --> 00:28:55.240
Who then, Larson, dragged him out of here?

00:28:56.070 --> 00:28:56.950
Just forget about it.

00:28:57.230 --> 00:28:58.990
Just mind your own business and you won't get into trouble.

00:29:00.380 --> 00:29:04.040
You're a decent guy, Hobbs. Why do you let things like this happen?

00:29:04.590 --> 00:29:07.870
There's nothing I can do about it. You can quit. You know this is bad.

00:29:08.500 --> 00:29:09.800
Why do you stand for all this?

00:29:09.920 --> 00:29:19.390
What are you so scared of? You ask too many...

00:31:03.960 --> 00:31:04.680
What are you doing here?

00:31:05.620 --> 00:31:06.680
Waiting for my wife.

00:31:06.820 --> 00:31:07.680
She's coming today.

00:31:08.200 --> 00:31:09.140
This is night.

00:31:10.250 --> 00:31:11.390
Go on back to your bed.

00:31:11.550 --> 00:31:13.610
If I see my wife, I might miss her.

00:31:14.520 --> 00:31:15.940
Go on back to your room.

00:31:44.620 --> 00:31:45.260
Feeling any better?

00:31:46.350 --> 00:31:46.590
No.

00:31:48.300 --> 00:31:49.160
Today's visitor's day.

00:31:49.280 --> 00:31:50.180
Anybody coming to see you?

00:31:50.570 --> 00:31:53.640
I don't think they're gonna let anybody see me like this.

00:31:58.430 --> 00:31:59.230
You're released from here.

00:32:01.720 --> 00:32:04.380
I have, a hundred times.

00:32:04.880 --> 00:32:07.060
What about your wife? Can't she get you out?

00:32:07.760 --> 00:32:09.760
They've got her convinced I'm dangerous.

00:32:10.080 --> 00:32:11.060
She believes them?

00:32:11.180 --> 00:32:13.650
They tell her it's better to keep me here

00:32:13.650 --> 00:32:14.970
than to go through a legal...

00:32:15.730 --> 00:32:18.690
that will publicize the fact her husband's crazy.

00:32:19.620 --> 00:32:24.940
You just relax. It'll take me a little time,

00:32:24.940 --> 00:32:28.310
but I'll get you out of here. Chin up.

00:32:40.780 --> 00:32:41.400
Larson today.

00:32:42.380 --> 00:32:42.640
Bye.

00:32:43.372 --> 00:32:44.892
He tore up some paper in the day room.

00:32:45.836 --> 00:32:48.456
Somebody ought to tell this kid's family this is no place for him.

00:32:49.100 --> 00:32:50.300
He doesn't have any family.

00:32:52.172 --> 00:32:54.172
You better get along. Your wife's waiting for you.

00:33:09.404 --> 00:33:09.644
Wow.

00:33:10.332 --> 00:33:12.332
He's beginning to act like a husband.

00:33:14.108 --> 00:33:14.868
It was kind of tough.

00:33:16.668 --> 00:33:18.668
You're really beginning to needle me.

00:33:22.940 --> 00:33:26.280
I know it must be a grim place, but just stick it out a little while longer.

00:33:26.360 --> 00:33:27.600
I'll stick it out. Don't worry.

00:33:30.670 --> 00:33:31.620
It's been a good night.

00:34:02.200 --> 00:34:04.840
You've got to get well soon, dear, so I can take you home.

00:34:05.240 --> 00:34:14.500
Deep, I don't think it's worth the risk.

00:34:15.090 --> 00:34:17.310
Forgetting that five grand a story.

00:34:19.920 --> 00:34:21.700
Not the money or the story anymore.

00:34:22.040 --> 00:34:24.170
I just don't want you to take any unnecessary...

00:34:30.220 --> 00:34:30.720
be around.

00:34:39.372 --> 00:34:39.992
Good afternoon.

00:34:42.220 --> 00:34:43.060
Good afternoon.

00:34:44.140 --> 00:34:45.140
Good afternoon.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:00.040
Thank you.

00:35:15.600 --> 00:35:20.030
Why isn't Topper cleaning up the locked ward?

00:35:20.280 --> 00:35:21.460
Oh, I needed some help.

00:35:21.480 --> 00:35:22.380
I'm the one that needs help.

00:35:22.760 --> 00:35:23.300
Send him upstairs.

00:35:33.580 --> 00:35:35.180
I think you better go upstairs.

00:35:35.468 --> 00:35:35.968
Yes.

00:35:36.396 --> 00:35:37.596
Thank you very much.

00:35:46.348 --> 00:35:46.908
Mr. Topper.

00:35:47.724 --> 00:35:48.224
Yes?

00:35:54.444 --> 00:35:54.704
Peace.

00:35:55.468 --> 00:35:55.968
Yes.

00:35:57.228 --> 00:35:58.228
Thank you.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:00.400
Thank you.

00:36:32.170 --> 00:36:34.400
Pops, I smell something burning.

00:37:01.120 --> 00:37:01.320
Thank you.

00:37:34.320 --> 00:37:35.500
Are you all right? Did you burn yourself?

00:37:35.900 --> 00:37:36.840
No, no, I'm okay.

00:37:38.070 --> 00:37:39.410
Well, come on. We have some more work to do.

00:37:39.590 --> 00:37:50.860
You got drunk and fell asleep with a lighted cigar. That's what happened.

00:37:51.680 --> 00:37:54.280
You think I'm going to stand by and let you ruin me and my place?

00:37:54.420 --> 00:37:56.460
I tell you, I wasn't smoking when I went to bed.

00:37:56.560 --> 00:37:58.280
How could you remember? You drank a quart of whiskey.

00:37:58.480 --> 00:37:59.980
That's my business. You're being well paid.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:00.760
for the little damage.

00:38:00.820 --> 00:38:02.780
I'm not being paid nearly enough to end up in jail.

00:38:03.620 --> 00:38:05.300
I made a deal with you, Judge, for one month.

00:38:05.640 --> 00:38:06.880
You've been here five weeks now.

00:38:07.120 --> 00:38:08.280
If you're not out of here in another week,

00:38:08.300 --> 00:38:09.260
I'll have to have more money.

00:38:10.170 --> 00:38:11.690
You're going to start bleeding me, eh, Porter?

00:38:12.180 --> 00:38:13.680
I'm running a great risk in furnishing you

00:38:13.680 --> 00:38:15.320
with the safest possible hideout you could have.

00:38:15.880 --> 00:38:17.380
I'm entitled to additional recompense.

00:38:17.500 --> 00:38:19.440
I'm not at all certain I'm as safe here

00:38:19.440 --> 00:38:20.300
as you seem to think.

00:38:20.760 --> 00:38:21.620
What are you talking about?

00:38:21.640 --> 00:38:22.160
Who is that patient?

00:38:22.320 --> 00:38:22.760
What patient?

00:38:22.880 --> 00:38:24.950
The one who helped put out the fire, Horton.

00:38:25.280 --> 00:38:26.960
He seemed very much interested in me.

00:38:28.020 --> 00:38:29.100
He's new here, isn't he?

00:38:29.240 --> 00:38:29.500
Yes.

00:38:30.120 --> 00:38:31.860
His wife had him committed with a letter

00:38:31.860 --> 00:38:32.740
from the state psychiatrist.

00:38:33.210 --> 00:38:34.150
I couldn't turn him down.

00:38:34.410 --> 00:38:35.870
I don't like the way he looked at me.

00:38:36.460 --> 00:38:38.800
You know, I caught Horton on the stairs here the other night.

00:38:39.060 --> 00:38:39.520
What night?

00:38:39.880 --> 00:38:42.680
Last Thursday, the night I brought Miss Bennett up to see you.

00:38:43.230 --> 00:38:45.050
And come to think of it, it happened once before, too.

00:38:45.790 --> 00:38:47.740
Look here, Porter, if you've let someone come.

00:38:48.520 --> 00:38:49.800
Look through Horton's stuff in his room.

00:38:50.220 --> 00:38:50.980
He'll be at lunch.

00:38:51.770 --> 00:38:52.550
I'll be in my office.

00:39:30.600 --> 00:39:31.400
Didn't find much.

00:39:31.520 --> 00:39:34.480
It's the usual stuff.

00:39:37.050 --> 00:39:38.190
Nothing here will tell us anything.

00:39:38.870 --> 00:39:40.470
Horton's record seems fairly authentic.

00:39:40.840 --> 00:39:43.720
Traveling salesman, unemployed, married, four years.

00:39:45.330 --> 00:39:46.650
He's married to a good-looking dame.

00:39:46.790 --> 00:39:55.290
How could we have been so stupid?

00:39:58.850 --> 00:39:59.970
This Horton is either a c-

00:40:00.840 --> 00:40:03.360
If the police are watching the sanitarium, we're all finished.

00:40:03.820 --> 00:40:05.800
You'll never be able to get out of here without being caught.

00:40:06.110 --> 00:40:08.130
Calm down. We've got to figure this thing out.

00:40:08.270 --> 00:40:09.990
What is there to figure it out? He knows you're here.

00:40:10.110 --> 00:40:11.310
It's only a question of time now.

00:40:11.550 --> 00:40:13.650
You're a stupid man when you get excited, Porter.

00:40:14.410 --> 00:40:17.310
Horton didn't know for sure that I was sharing to the fire a little while ago.

00:40:17.660 --> 00:40:20.340
He hasn't been able to communicate that information to anyone yet.

00:40:20.440 --> 00:40:22.060
His wife will be here to see him this afternoon.

00:40:22.490 --> 00:40:24.090
Obviously, she can't be allowed to see him.

00:40:24.480 --> 00:40:26.260
She's a part of this scheme of Horton's.

00:40:26.400 --> 00:40:28.060
She's the one we've got to worry about now.

00:40:28.360 --> 00:40:29.980
I was crazy ever to let you come.

00:40:30.410 --> 00:40:32.400
I'll lose my place. Go to jail.

00:40:32.800 --> 00:40:33.880
You won't lose a thing.

00:40:34.180 --> 00:40:35.540
All you have to do is get rid of Horton.

00:40:36.240 --> 00:40:37.800
I'll get out of here tonight with Madge,

00:40:37.880 --> 00:40:40.620
and there's no way for anyone to prove that I was ever in here.

00:40:40.940 --> 00:40:41.980
How do we get rid of Horton?

00:40:42.400 --> 00:40:44.020
Well, that shouldn't be too hard to figure out.

00:40:44.460 --> 00:40:45.520
The champ could take care of him.

00:40:46.380 --> 00:40:47.640
That's not a bad idea.

00:40:48.490 --> 00:40:50.290
You could make out a report that he was attacked

00:40:50.290 --> 00:40:52.790
by one of the violent patients and died of the effects.

00:40:53.310 --> 00:40:53.830
That's murder.

00:40:56.250 --> 00:40:57.890
I bargained for murder when I went into this with you.

00:40:58.320 --> 00:40:59.980
You have a choice between that or...

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:00.880
or jail and ruin.

00:41:01.060 --> 00:41:07.190
Just wait until tonight, when all the visitors

00:41:07.190 --> 00:41:07.930
are off the premises.

00:41:08.690 --> 00:41:10.270
Better have Horton locked up.

00:41:10.980 --> 00:41:12.480
You'll have to give his wife a story

00:41:12.480 --> 00:41:13.560
why she can't see him today.

00:41:14.120 --> 00:41:15.700
Maybe we'd better lock her up, too.

00:41:15.880 --> 00:41:16.880
Don't be ridiculous.

00:41:17.470 --> 00:41:18.890
That would really tip our mitt.

00:41:19.660 --> 00:41:20.300
Just stall her.

00:41:20.720 --> 00:41:21.280
I'll handle it.

00:41:22.330 --> 00:41:23.750
Get those things back to Horton's locker.

00:41:24.240 --> 00:41:26.040
We don't want him to know yet that we found him out.

00:41:39.950 --> 00:41:40.410
What's wrong?

00:41:40.710 --> 00:41:41.390
Lose something?

00:41:42.240 --> 00:41:42.540
Yeah.

00:41:48.470 --> 00:41:50.110
We found one of the patients with these.

00:41:50.290 --> 00:41:51.210
Porter says they're yours.

00:41:52.980 --> 00:41:53.260
Yeah.

00:41:54.100 --> 00:41:56.100
You got to keep your stuff locked up around here.

00:41:56.860 --> 00:41:57.380
I can see that.

00:41:58.750 --> 00:41:59.910
I'm going to need you for a few minutes.

00:42:01.730 --> 00:42:03.730
Saturday. I gotta change my clothes. My wife's coming.

00:42:04.310 --> 00:42:08.760
You have an hour yet. I gotta get the locked ward clean up. Come on.

00:42:33.960 --> 00:42:36.560
Before you start washing these walls, I want you to clean up this room.

00:42:36.720 --> 00:42:40.840
I need some help if I'm to be done in time for...

00:42:40.840 --> 00:42:42.720
You'll have plenty of time. Stop your cribbing.

00:42:42.860 --> 00:42:43.720
You're not gonna miss anything.

00:43:25.460 --> 00:43:27.080
Dr. Porter would like to see you, please.

00:43:30.160 --> 00:43:30.480
Please.

00:43:37.460 --> 00:43:38.560
Mrs. Horton, doctor.

00:43:41.350 --> 00:43:42.290
Good afternoon, doctor.

00:43:42.630 --> 00:43:43.470
Hello, Mrs. Horton.

00:43:45.300 --> 00:43:46.020
Won't you sit down?

00:43:54.320 --> 00:43:55.520
Is something wrong, doctor?

00:43:56.550 --> 00:43:58.150
I have some most regrettable news.

00:44:00.440 --> 00:44:01.860
Your husband has had an accident.

00:44:02.260 --> 00:44:04.680
He was apparently wandering around the building last night

00:44:04.680 --> 00:44:07.260
and somehow got into the locked ward with the violent patients.

00:44:07.480 --> 00:44:08.040
What happened, Doc?

00:44:08.140 --> 00:44:09.860
He was attacked and pretty badly beaten.

00:44:10.880 --> 00:44:12.680
Believe me, Mrs. Horton, we are extremely

00:44:12.680 --> 00:44:13.940
sorry that this has happened.

00:44:15.170 --> 00:44:17.190
Can't understand how he got into the locked ward

00:44:17.190 --> 00:44:18.030
without being seen.

00:44:19.690 --> 00:44:20.770
May I see him, Doctor?

00:44:21.090 --> 00:44:22.430
That wouldn't be advisable, my dear.

00:44:22.490 --> 00:44:24.770
He's suffering from shock and shouldn't be disturbed at all.

00:44:24.850 --> 00:44:26.030
Oh, just to look in on him.

00:44:26.180 --> 00:44:29.980
To be quite frank, Mrs. Horton, he's been rather badly hurt.

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:33.880
As soon as this condition warrants, I'll call you and you can see him.

00:44:34.960 --> 00:44:40.220
All right. You'll let me know tomorrow how he is.

00:44:40.550 --> 00:44:42.110
I'll call you myself in the morning.

00:44:43.800 --> 00:44:47.180
Let me say again that I'm extremely sorry that this has happened.

00:44:47.360 --> 00:44:50.260
However, I'm sure that he'll come around all right.

00:44:51.130 --> 00:44:51.550
Thank you.

00:45:10.010 --> 00:45:14.380
Say, Larson, Burton hasn't been in here all day.

00:45:14.540 --> 00:45:16.060
He's not in his room, and I thought it was.

00:45:16.060 --> 00:45:16.680
He's all right.

00:45:17.000 --> 00:45:17.900
Never mind about him.

00:45:18.280 --> 00:45:25.490
Yeah, but you're going to learn to stop messing up this place.

00:45:26.580 --> 00:45:27.600
Don't you ever hit him.

00:45:28.030 --> 00:45:29.270
I'll take care of what he does.

00:45:29.650 --> 00:45:29.970
You'll be right.

00:45:30.060 --> 00:45:30.780
I bet you will.

00:45:31.270 --> 00:45:33.550
I'm getting sick and tired of this kid of yours

00:45:33.550 --> 00:45:34.910
messing up the place every day.

00:45:36.000 --> 00:45:38.080
I don't know why Porter let you both stay here.

00:45:39.340 --> 00:45:42.900
Now on, I'm going to hold you responsible for anything he does.

00:45:43.350 --> 00:45:45.650
Don't you ever lay a hand on my boy again.

00:45:46.380 --> 00:45:48.810
Yeah? What can you do about it?

00:45:50.080 --> 00:45:51.000
You're no good, Larson.

00:45:52.430 --> 00:45:53.530
You'll get yours someday.

00:45:55.680 --> 00:45:56.520
You'll get yours.

00:45:57.320 --> 00:45:59.400
Larson, come with me.

00:46:11.960 --> 00:46:13.920
Mrs. Horton has been very nicely taken care of.

00:46:14.880 --> 00:46:18.020
I told her that her husband was attacked by another patient last night

00:46:18.020 --> 00:46:20.240
and his condition was too critical for her to see him today.

00:46:20.800 --> 00:46:21.980
Are you sure she believed you?

00:46:22.160 --> 00:46:23.920
Positive. She seemed quite stunned.

00:46:25.730 --> 00:46:29.940
You know, I'd like to find out who...

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:31.940
what Horton is before you take care of him.

00:46:32.060 --> 00:46:32.820
Let's get him in here.

00:46:33.230 --> 00:46:35.130
After all, we're not keeping any secrets from him now.

00:46:35.830 --> 00:46:36.430
How will he do that?

00:46:36.550 --> 00:46:37.810
I don't want to interrupt us raised.

00:46:47.540 --> 00:46:49.080
I wonder how Horton knew you were here.

00:46:49.790 --> 00:46:52.090
Do you think he found out about Madge and followed her?

00:46:52.310 --> 00:46:53.230
I don't think so.

00:46:54.370 --> 00:46:55.750
Madge is a pretty clever girl.

00:46:56.670 --> 00:46:58.830
However, I don't see how that could do him any good now.

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:01.380
I see you're being mighty calm about it.

00:47:02.470 --> 00:47:04.070
I think we're in hot water up to our necks.

00:47:04.150 --> 00:47:04.970
Up to whose necks?

00:47:11.070 --> 00:47:11.690
Sit down, Horton.

00:47:11.850 --> 00:47:17.070
Whatever your name is.

00:47:20.460 --> 00:47:21.100
And who are you?

00:47:23.300 --> 00:47:23.640
I'll get you.

00:47:24.240 --> 00:47:27.720
You will, Carson.

00:47:32.170 --> 00:47:34.790
Let's not waste time. We know you're not really here as a patient.

00:47:35.030 --> 00:47:36.310
Who are you? Who sent you here?

00:47:36.660 --> 00:47:38.260
I'm Harry Horton, my wife sent me.

00:47:38.500 --> 00:47:40.180
I'd advise you to tell us what we want to know.

00:47:40.260 --> 00:47:42.100
Otherwise, things may become very unpleasant for you.

00:47:42.100 --> 00:47:43.560
I still don't know what you're talking about.

00:47:44.210 --> 00:47:47.030
Oh, that picture of mine on the back of your wife's photo?

00:47:47.660 --> 00:47:49.360
I told your wife this afternoon

00:47:49.360 --> 00:47:52.060
that you've been very badly beaten by a violent patient.

00:47:53.010 --> 00:47:56.270
Ain't she gonna be sad when she finds out you die from your injuries?

00:47:56.430 --> 00:47:57.690
Keep your stupid mouth shut.

00:47:57.890 --> 00:47:59.430
Who are you? Who's in this with you?

00:48:01.400 --> 00:48:02.840
The entire police force, Porter.

00:48:05.970 --> 00:48:06.870
I think he's lying.

00:48:07.370 --> 00:48:08.390
You'll find out any minute.

00:48:08.890 --> 00:48:11.750
My wife must have reported my supposed accident by now.

00:48:12.000 --> 00:48:12.860
Apparently she didn't.

00:48:13.200 --> 00:48:15.820
She left here over two hours ago and we haven't heard any more about it.

00:48:15.960 --> 00:48:17.120
You will, Porter, you will.

00:48:17.940 --> 00:48:21.240
And if you boys are smart, you won't make it any tougher for yourselves than you need to.

00:48:22.590 --> 00:48:25.990
Accidents are quite likely to happen in a mental sanitarium, my friend.

00:48:31.950 --> 00:48:35.130
This is absolutely the most fantastic story I've ever heard.

00:48:35.580 --> 00:48:36.340
It's incredible.

00:48:36.600 --> 00:48:37.560
I suppose it is.

00:48:38.310 --> 00:48:39.730
You've made a fool out of me.

00:48:40.460 --> 00:48:42.800
Involved me in a situation that is most unethical.

00:48:43.650 --> 00:48:45.520
And now, you want me to help you.

00:48:45.830 --> 00:48:47.550
We felt that Porter might be suspicious

00:48:47.550 --> 00:48:49.870
unless we came to him with some professional opinion.

00:48:50.420 --> 00:48:52.760
You thought nothing of degrading my professional reputation.

00:48:53.260 --> 00:48:54.360
I'm sorry, Doctor.

00:48:55.430 --> 00:48:56.430
But if Judge Drake isn't...

00:48:56.430 --> 00:48:59.980
If he's in there, has Horton or Stewart or whatever his name is...

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:01.920
actually found Judge Drake in there?

00:49:02.840 --> 00:49:03.260
I don't know.

00:49:03.900 --> 00:49:06.040
You're accusing this Dr. Porter of a criminal act.

00:49:06.220 --> 00:49:07.200
You have no proof.

00:49:08.010 --> 00:49:10.030
Stuart may actually have been attacked by a patient.

00:49:10.310 --> 00:49:11.070
I don't think so.

00:49:11.820 --> 00:49:13.800
I think both of you have acted stupidly and rashly.

00:49:14.050 --> 00:49:16.170
Well, all right, doctor, but that isn't the point now.

00:49:17.870 --> 00:49:19.390
If you won't help me, I'd better go to the police.

00:49:20.060 --> 00:49:22.300
I don't think the police would barge in on a private sanitarium,

00:49:22.920 --> 00:49:24.060
merely on your suspicions.

00:49:24.680 --> 00:49:26.700
They'd let themselves wide open for a civil suit.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:31.300
I think you're needlessly worried about it.

00:49:32.290 --> 00:49:34.540
I'd advise you to go out there tomorrow or the next day.

00:49:35.070 --> 00:49:37.190
Take him out of the sanitarium and forget the whole thing.

00:49:37.330 --> 00:49:38.470
Tomorrow may be too late.

00:49:38.960 --> 00:49:41.520
Well, frankly, Mrs., I don't know what I can do for him.

00:49:45.060 --> 00:49:45.880
Have to excuse me.

00:49:46.440 --> 00:49:47.960
It's after 6, and I have a dinner engaged.

00:50:44.140 --> 00:50:44.560
Come on, Horton.

00:51:05.020 --> 00:51:05.740
You guys kidding?

00:51:21.640 --> 00:51:22.320
Wait a minute, champ.

00:52:30.990 --> 00:52:32.010
He ain't gone anyplace.

00:53:37.680 --> 00:53:38.280
What are you doing here?

00:53:40.340 --> 00:53:40.820
Nothing, sir.

00:53:41.040 --> 00:53:42.880
I have some work to do.

00:53:43.300 --> 00:53:44.520
Get out of here and stay out.

00:53:46.130 --> 00:53:46.530
Yes, sir.

00:53:49.540 --> 00:53:50.280
Lock that door.

00:54:30.030 --> 00:54:31.630
All right, all right, what do you want?

00:54:32.630 --> 00:54:34.750
Pull over to the curb when you get past the main gate.

00:54:36.000 --> 00:54:38.080
Stop the car and throw the keys in the back seat.

00:55:28.190 --> 00:55:29.970
If you don't struggle too much, the ropes won't hurt.

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:30.020
Thank you.

00:56:01.530 --> 00:56:01.910
Thank you.

00:56:36.720 --> 00:56:39.450
We've got trouble. Found a guy in here as a patient looking for the judge.

00:56:40.060 --> 00:56:41.000
The judge is getting packed.

00:56:41.720 --> 00:56:43.580
We got everything fixed so nobody gets in a jam.

00:57:03.580 --> 00:57:04.280
Miss Bennett, Judge.

00:57:04.640 --> 00:57:04.760
Yeah.

00:57:11.560 --> 00:57:12.080
Right, Madge.

00:57:14.360 --> 00:57:15.480
Did Larson tell you what happened?

00:57:21.550 --> 00:57:22.310
Put your hands down.

00:57:22.450 --> 00:57:23.810
Get Harry Horton in here right away.

00:57:24.070 --> 00:57:25.250
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:57:25.310 --> 00:57:25.610
Get him.

00:57:30.760 --> 00:57:31.180
Larson.

00:57:32.390 --> 00:57:32.870
Yes, sir?

00:57:33.360 --> 00:57:34.200
Bring Horton in here.

00:57:34.600 --> 00:57:35.820
Dr. Porter said to leave.

00:57:35.860 --> 00:57:36.540
Bring him in here.

00:57:46.700 --> 00:57:47.340
Easy temp.

00:57:49.470 --> 00:57:50.170
Easy boy.

00:57:51.050 --> 00:57:53.320
Horton, Horton.

00:57:58.380 --> 00:57:58.960
Easy temp.

00:58:10.880 --> 00:58:11.280
Hurry up.

00:58:14.130 --> 00:58:28.070
Hold it.

00:58:38.160 --> 00:58:39.180
You're a wife and a million.

00:58:39.400 --> 00:58:40.460
Give me that gun.

00:58:40.880 --> 00:58:41.700
Can you make it all right?

00:58:41.720 --> 00:58:42.540
I can make it, baby.

00:58:43.580 --> 00:58:45.080
All right, Larson, open that door.

00:58:46.700 --> 00:58:49.850
Wide going, Judge.

00:58:53.590 --> 00:58:54.370
It's not locked that much.

00:59:00.860 --> 00:59:01.100
Thank you.

00:59:50.920 --> 00:59:54.870
All right, bud, drop it.

00:59:57.500 --> 00:59:58.920
I'm Ross Stewart, private detective.

00:59:59.060 --> 00:59:59.980
I imagine you know my...

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:01.200
my friend, Judge Finley Drake?

01:00:01.630 --> 01:00:02.470
I certainly do.

01:00:02.730 --> 01:00:04.630
Over by the wall, Judge, with your hands in the air.

01:00:05.940 --> 01:00:07.180
Looks like you had quite a party.

01:00:07.320 --> 01:00:09.020
We did indeed, and we couldn't be happier

01:00:09.020 --> 01:00:10.220
that you boys were invited.

01:00:10.380 --> 01:00:10.620
But who?

01:00:11.160 --> 01:00:12.710
I called them.

01:00:12.840 --> 01:00:13.860
You, Hobbs.

01:00:14.040 --> 01:00:14.960
You're a man of action.

01:00:15.060 --> 01:00:16.080
I never thought you had it in you.

01:00:16.960 --> 01:00:17.700
Neither did I.

01:00:18.260 --> 01:00:19.380
I'd better call my paper.

01:00:25.340 --> 01:00:26.300
He's a nice guy.

01:00:27.390 --> 01:00:28.210
Hang on to him.

01:00:31.150 --> 01:00:33.020
Operator, long distance, please.

01:00:42.240 --> 01:00:43.840
Operator, long distance, please.

01:00:48.600 --> 01:00:50.020
Sorry, darling, my job.

01:00:50.160 --> 01:00:52.080
I never like to start anything I can't finish.

01:00:54.760 --> 01:00:55.060
Why?

01:01:01.300 --> 01:01:02.040
Operator.

01:01:04.030 --> 01:01:05.290
Oh, excuse me.

01:01:09.350 --> 01:01:10.610
I never did think he was crazy.
